WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.300
Welcome to Cloud Minute!

00:00:01.300 --> 00:00:03.900
Today I'm going to show you a bit about Stackdriver Error Reporting.

00:00:04.333 --> 00:00:07.266
Like most folks I occasionally ship code that has bugs in it.

00:00:07.533 --> 00:00:09.200
Luckily Error Reporting can help me out.

00:00:09.700 --> 00:00:13.033
So I just got an email tellling me that there's a new error in my App Engine app.

00:00:13.566 --> 00:00:16.366
I deployed a couple minutes ago so the error is probably related.

00:00:17.666 --> 00:00:21.166
It looks like there is a division by zero error that is causing a 500 response.

00:00:21.433 --> 00:00:23.766
I can go to the cloud console to get more details.

00:00:26.266 --> 00:00:27.233
Once on the console 

00:00:27.233 --> 00:00:31.500
I can see that this error has happened nine times and that it's been seen in multiple versions of my application.

00:00:32.100 --> 00:00:33.233
I can see the status that it's

00:00:33.233 --> 00:00:36.833
causing and I can also see when the error was first seen and when it was last seen.

00:00:37.600 --> 00:00:39.333
If I scroll down a little bit there's some samples

00:00:39.333 --> 00:00:42.333
of the error that include a stack trace and some additional

00:00:42.333 --> 00:00:44.366
information that might be helpful for debugging.

00:00:45.400 --> 00:00:48.233
Usually in my process at this point I'd enter a bug.

00:00:48.666 --> 00:00:49.733
And once I do that I can link a bug to this error by clicking this button.

00:00:52.700 --> 00:00:56.000
I hope Error Reporting is able to help you fix application errors quickly.

